{
 "answer": {
  "answer": "The study confirmed only 2 of the 5 cases it was after, so the goal was not met. Both confirmed cases failed on every kept run. Each range lies just above 0.5, so they are confirmed, but only narrowly. The first is scene 023b7fcc with the lead car moved 1.5 s earlier at 0.5x speed and the ego at its recorded speed (S1). Here the policy takes over already close behind a slow lead car and does not brake hard enough. The second is scene 096988dd with the car at its recorded timing, 1.5x car speed and the ego at 1.4x (S7). Here the policy drifts left out of its lane and sideswipes a car beside it, which is not the retimed car. A third case on 096988dd failed the same way but ran only once, so it is a hint rather than a rate (S5). No setting on the other seven scenes that ran failed, and one scene in the plan was never run.",
  "findings": [
   {
    "claim": "On 023b7fcc, moving the lead car 1.5 s earlier at 0.5x speed, with the ego at its recorded speed, makes the policy hit the lead car's rear on every run, and the range lies above 0.5. The triage reads this as a failure to brake: the ego takes over a few metres behind a slower car, eases off only gently and runs into it. A rear hit from the car behind came after the front collision each time. For one run, triage marked the policy's fault as unclear, because the gap at hand-off was about 1 m.",
    "settings": [
     "S1"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On 023b7fcc this failure looks sensitive to the car's timing. At 1.0 s earlier, with the same car speed and ego speed, the single run did not fail and did not come close. One run is not enough to locate the edge.",
    "settings": [
     "S1",
     "S2"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On 096988dd, a faster car (1.5x) at its recorded timing combined with a faster ego (1.4x) fails on every run, and the range lies above 0.5. In each run the policy steered left of its route into the next lane and hit actor 41 front-on or side-on. Actor 41 is not the retimed car (track 2), so the policy's lane keeping caused these failures, not the retimed car's cut-in.",
    "settings": [
     "S7"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "096988dd also failed in its single run with the car 2 s earlier at 1.25x and the ego at its recorded speed, in the same way (drifting left into actor 41). With a slower car and a slower ego (0.5x, 0.8x) it did not fail but came close. This suggests the drift-left failure happens across much of this scene, not just at one combination.",
    "settings": [
     "S5",
     "S6",
     "S7"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "Several repeated settings on other scenes did not fail on any run, and their ranges lie below 0.5. These include 09a95ffa (car 0.5 s later, 1.5x, ego 0.8x), 12855a41 (recorded timing, ego 1.4x; and car 0.5x, ego 0.6x), 19f339ba (car 2 s later at 0.75x or 1.25x), 0e899dd3 (car 1 s earlier; car 2 s later at 1.25x with ego 1.2x) and 0cf6368d (car 1 s later at 2x, ego 1.4x).",
    "settings": [
     "S11",
     "S27",
     "S28",
     "S32",
     "S33",
     "S21",
     "S25",
     "S15"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "The closest calls without a collision were on 19f339ba, 096988dd, 09a95ffa and 0e899dd3. By the brief's ranking these near misses come next after the two confirmed cases.",
    "settings": [
     "S32",
     "S6",
     "S31",
     "S33",
     "S12",
     "S25"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On 0dbb91dd the ego never came close to another actor in any setting tried, even though as recorded it came within 0.23 m. The ranges for single runs are wide, so this scene is not cleared.",
    "settings": [
     "S16",
     "S17",
     "S18",
     "S19"
    ]
   }
  ],
  "open": [
   "Three more confirmed cases on different scenes are still missing. Scene 187e6244 is in the plan but was never run. 1c45ce3a had only one kept run; a second (car 1.5 s later, 2x, ego 1.4x) halted and was not kept.",
   "Whether the single failure on 096988dd (car 2 s earlier, 1.25x, ego 1.0x) repeats. Repeating it would only add a second case on the same scene, so it would not count towards the goal. Running 096988dd at the recorded car timing and speed with ego 1.4x would show whether the ego's speed alone causes the drift left into actor 41.",
   "Where the failure edge lies on 023b7fcc between the car 1.5 s and 1.0 s earlier, and whether the faster ego speeds fail too. Repeats at -1.0 s and at -1.5 s with ego 1.2x would show this.",
   "Whether the near misses on 19f339ba (car 0.5x, ego 1.2x), 09a95ffa (car 1.5 s later, 1.25x, ego 1.2x) and 0e899dd3 tip into failure at harsher neighbouring settings, such as an earlier car timing or a faster ego. Each needs several repeats before it can count as confirmed."
  ]
